# Test lanes

- Structural fixtures exercise production visitors and explicit occurrence
  selectors without compilers. Expected correspondence is independently authored.
- Authored provider fixtures qualify joins, not native semantics. Live native
  controls are opt-in; missing tools remain unavailable, never a passing result.
- Storage/application tests own transactions, restart, producer isolation and
  CLI/MCP behavior. Campaign measurements do not replace correctness tests.
- Keep focused fixtures together; remove obsolete tests and consumers together.
  Raw outputs and exact receipts are optional when they offer no practical value.
- Maintain [test ownership](../../scripts/test_ownership.json); shared changes run
  representative families and full workspace checks. C++ remains experimental.
- Scratch belongs in `.tmp/<task>/`. Test-only temporary directories are disposable.
  Details: [testing runbook](../../docs/runbooks/testing.md).
